<article class="env-lemma" id="0FK3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FK3">Lemma <span data-tag="0FK3">37.62.17</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of finite presentation. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is a local complete intersection morphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is syntomic, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}$ has tor-amplitude in $[-1, 0]$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}$ is perfect with tor-amplitude in $[-1, 0]$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Translated into algebra this is Divided Power Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FJV" data-tag="0FJV">23.11.5</a>. To do the translation use Lemmas <a href="/tag/07DB" data-tag="07DB">37.62.5</a> and <a href="/tag/0D0I" data-tag="0D0I">37.13.2</a> as well as Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/06Z0" data-tag="06Z0">36.3.5</a>, <a href="/tag/08E9" data-tag="08E9">36.10.4</a> and <a href="/tag/08EB" data-tag="08EB">36.10.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>